nnel_mode % 4` happens *before* the switch, so `TFLAC_CHANNEL_MODE_COUNT` (4) behaves as `INDEPENDENT`, `255` as `MID_SIDE`, and the `default:` arm is unreachable. Verified for all 256 `u8` values.\n\n## Exhaustive proof\n\nSince each axis ORs into a disjoint bit range, I swept **all four `u32` axes over their complete `2^32` domain** (~17.2B full-struct comparisons, 69 s), plus all 256 `channel_mode` values crossed with `channels` boundaries — **all clean**.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: `t == NULL` is documented but *not* executed (both sides SIGSEGV identically; a crash isn't differentially comparable), and `cargo` needed `--offline` as the proxy blocked crates.io — `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local cache."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":96243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1076,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd51f9ce-4be5-4292-8835-53ca42d5f959","uuid":"de7322ee-bebb-49e3-91e6-10f97506114c","timestamp":"2026-09-05T02:32:34.934Z"}
